//@version=6
// WAR FORMATION E91 -- E90's QUEUE ITEM 1: POPULATION COUNTER, 6h-BLOCK-EXTREME REFERENCE.
//
// SCHEDULING NOTE. This cycle's stored prompt again describes lab state that is long closed
// (1m-only data window, "attack the short's entry geometry via E64a/E64b/E66," "continue numbering
// after E66"). That family finished at E70/E76/E77 (entry-term binding) and E71/E74-E79 (short
// geometry) many cycles ago; E81, E89 and E90 already flagged this exact same staleness in their own
// headers. The docs win, per the prompt's own instruction and this lab's own repeated precedent: this
// cycle continues E90's own queue item 1, its own top, explicitly-named-next item -- "re-attempt
// HARD LESSON 41's target-a-level idea with the current 6h block's own running high/low ... as the TP
// reference instead of the prior 1h bucket's ... Count ITS population with a counter build (same
// method as E90) BEFORE spending a credit on the strategy version."
//
// STATE FOR THE RECORD: no champion, no candidate anywhere in the lab. e58a (long, 1m, PF
// 1.24015239, DD 9.82519609%, 36 trades) and E71 (short, 1m) are the confirmed-reproducible 1m-track
// reference builds, untouched. E80/E82 (15m, maxBars=288) and E87 (15m, maxBars=576) sit at status:
// research (both looked like edges on the full window, both failed a split test). E89's level-target
// redesign against the prior-1h-bucket reference (p1hh/p1hl) returned ZERO trades; E90 measured why --
// 93.3% of the population's reward distance sits under $500, and NONE reaches even $1,500, because the
// reclaim trigger fires the instant price re-crosses the level, so the opposite extreme of the SAME
// already-swept 1h bucket is inherently close by. E90's own queue named the one live alternative left:
// the PRIOR completed 6h block's own high/low -- six times wider a window than the 1h bucket E90 just
// measured as an order of magnitude too small, and (unlike the CURRENT still-forming bucket, which
// would be look-ahead) fully known and available the instant the new 6h block starts, at the same
// bucket transition that already produces grnPrev/cntPrev for bullRegime/bearRegime.
//
// THIS RUN MEASURES THAT WIDER DISTANCE DIRECTLY, IN ONE CREDIT, BEFORE ANY STRATEGY VERSION IS BUILT
// -- per E90's queue item 1's own instruction not to repeat E89's process error (building the strategy
// before counting the population).
//
// METHOD: byte-identical to E90 in every respect except the reward-distance reference. New state is
// added -- c6hh/c6hl (the CURRENT 6h block's running high/low, updated every bar, mirroring the
// existing c1hh/c1hl pattern) and p6hh/p6hl (the PRIOR COMPLETED 6h block's high/low, captured at the
// same `if new6` transition that already captures grnPrev/cntPrev, so no look-ahead: by the time
// regimeReady allows a trade, the block p6hh/p6hl describes has fully finished). rewardDist becomes
// `p6hh - close` for longs, `close - p6hl` for shorts. Six $500-wide bins, same edges as E90, encoded
// as qty (0.01-0.06) so get_trades (a free read after this one paid run) recovers the full binned
// distribution and the long/short split from a single credit, exactly as E90 did.
//
// PRE-RUN AUDIT:
//   Not a strategy candidate -- no R floor, no stop-placement, no BINDING-as-a-strategy audit
//   applies (same exemption E81/E90 recorded for themselves).
//   BINDING (E17): goLong/goShort are byte-identical to e82-e80-no-h1bull-h1bear.pine (the same
//     population E90 measured) -- the ONLY change from E90 is the rewardDist reference and the new
//     c6hh/c6hl/p6hh/p6hl state that feeds it. atr periods, shieldUsd is not used here (no strategy
//     risk applies to a counter build), coilK, velK, the whole-number band, timeGate, witching-hour
//     ban -- all untouched.
//   REDUNDANCY (HARD LESSON 18): c6hh/c6hl/p6hh/p6hl ARE new state -- E90's queue text's parenthetical
//     ("already computed for bullRegime/bearRegime, no new state") is corrected here: bullRegime/
//     bearRegime read grnPrev/cntPrev (a green-candle COUNT), not a price extreme: no 6h high/low
//     tracker existed anywhere in this lab's 15m pine before this file. The new state is the minimum
//     needed to answer the question and follows the SAME bucket-transition pattern already proven
//     correct for c1hh/c1hl/p1hh/p1hl, applied to b6 instead of b1h.
//   Latch order (LESSON 8): p6hh/p6hl are captured in the SAME `if new6` block, BEFORE grnCur/cntCur
//     reset and before c6hh/c6hl are reseeded to the new block's first bar -- same ordering discipline
//     as the existing 1h capture.
//   OCCUPANCY CONFOUND (HARD LESSON 24/28/29): not applicable -- 1-bar-hold counter, no held position.
//
// REGISTERED PREDICTION (HARD LESSON 17), BEFORE RUNNING:
//   (a) A completed 6h block spans 6x the bars of the 1h bucket E90 measured, so its own high-low
//       range should be several times wider on typical BTC volatility -- predict the distribution
//       shifts materially off the E90 floor, with a non-trivial share (not necessarily a majority)
//       clearing $1,500-2,000 and some reaching $2,000-2,500 or beyond, naming a workable minRRv
//       against a $2,000 shield (roughly 0.75-1.5) where E90's reference offered none.
//   (b) IF the distribution is STILL concentrated under $500-1000 despite the 6x-wider window, that
//       would mean the binding constraint is not bucket width but where in the block the entry sits
//       (structurally close to the swept level by construction of brokeBelow/brokeAbove +
//       longTrig/shortTrig), which would close the level-target line on this 15m track entirely
//       rather than merely naming a smaller minRRv -- a different, harder conclusion than (a).
//   Both outcomes are informative; this is a genuine measurement, not a foregone conclusion.
//
// RESULT and interpretation are recorded in EXPERIMENT-LOG.md and results/backtests.json after this
// run completes, per the lab's provenance rule (never hand-write a metric).
strategy("WF E91 6h-block reward-distance population counter", overlay=true,
     pyramiding=1, process_orders_on_close=true,
     commission_type=strategy.commission.percent, commission_value=0.05,
     initial_capital=50000,
     default_qty_type=strategy.percent_of_equity, default_qty_value=100,
     margin_long=100, margin_short=100)

greenBull = input.int(4,     "Green 1h candles for BULL")
greenBear = input.int(2,     "Green 1h candles at or below for BEAR")
skipOpen  = input.int(60,    "Skip first N minutes of 6h block")
skipClose = input.int(60,    "Skip last N minutes of 6h block")
coilK     = input.float(0.85,"Coil: atrFast < atrSlow * K")
velK      = input.float(0.8, "Velocity: min reclaim as multiple of atrSlow")
midLo     = input.float(400, "Whole-number middles low")
midHi     = input.float(600, "Whole-number middles high")
etOffset  = input.int(-4,    "ET offset from UTC")
witchOn   = input.bool(true, "Ban longs in witching hour 1-4am ET")

MS6H = 21600000
MS1H = 3600000

b6  = math.floor(time / MS6H)
b1h = math.floor(time / MS1H)

new6  = b6  != b6[1]
new1h = b1h != b1h[1]

var float h1o     = na
var int   grnCur  = 0
var int   cntCur  = 0
var int   grnPrev = 0
var int   cntPrev = 0

// NEW STATE (E91): the 6h block's own running and prior-completed high/low, captured at the same
// bucket transition as grnPrev/cntPrev -- p6hh/p6hl describe a block that has FULLY FINISHED by the
// time the current block's bars are being evaluated, so this is not look-ahead.
var float c6hh = na
var float c6hl = na
var float p6hh = na
var float p6hl = na

if new6
    grnPrev := grnCur
    cntPrev := cntCur
    p6hh    := c6hh
    p6hl    := c6hl
    grnCur  := 0
    cntCur  := 0
    c6hh    := high
    c6hl    := low
else
    c6hh := na(c6hh) ? high : math.max(c6hh, high)
    c6hl := na(c6hl) ? low  : math.min(c6hl, low)

if new1h
    if not na(h1o)
        cntCur := cntCur + 1
        if close[1] > h1o
            grnCur := grnCur + 1
    h1o := open

regimeReady = cntPrev >= 5
bullRegime  = regimeReady and grnPrev >= greenBull
bearRegime  = regimeReady and grnPrev <= greenBear

minsIn    = (time - b6 * MS6H) / 60000
timeGate  = minsIn >= skipOpen and minsIn <= (360 - skipClose)

var float c1hh = na
var float c1hl = na
var float p1hh = na
var float p1hl = na

if new1h
    p1hh := c1hh
    p1hl := c1hl
    c1hh := high
    c1hl := low
else
    c1hh := na(c1hh) ? high : math.max(c1hh, high)
    c1hl := na(c1hl) ? low  : math.min(c1hl, low)

brokeBelow = not na(p1hl) and c1hl < p1hl
brokeAbove = not na(p1hh) and c1hh > p1hh

atrFast = ta.atr(1)
atrSlow = ta.atr(2)
coiled  = not na(atrSlow) and atrSlow > 0 and atrFast < atrSlow * coilK
coilPrev = coiled[1]
velMin   = na(atrSlow) ? na : atrSlow * velK

sub      = close - math.floor(close / 1000) * 1000
inMiddle = sub >= midLo and sub <= midHi

hUTC     = math.floor(time / MS1H) % 24
hET      = (hUTC + etOffset + 24) % 24
witching = hET >= 1 and hET < 4
longBan  = witchOn and witching

longTrig  = not na(p1hl) and not na(velMin) and ta.crossover(close, p1hl)  and (close - p1hl) >= velMin
shortTrig = not na(p1hh) and not na(velMin) and ta.crossunder(close, p1hh) and (p1hh - close) >= velMin

// BYTE-IDENTICAL to e82-e80-no-h1bull-h1bear.pine's (and E90's) goLong/goShort -- the exact same
// population, so this run's distribution is directly comparable to E90's bin counts, term for term.
goLong  = bullRegime and timeGate and brokeBelow and coilPrev and not inMiddle and not longBan and longTrig
goShort = bearRegime and timeGate and brokeAbove and coilPrev and not inMiddle and shortTrig

// THE MEASUREMENT (changed from E90): reward distance to the PRIOR COMPLETED 6h block's own extreme,
// not the prior 1h bucket's.
rewardDist = goLong ? (p6hh - close) : goShort ? (close - p6hl) : na

// Same six $500-wide bins as E90, encoded as qty so get_trades reports the bin without extra credit.
// qty = binNumber / 100 (0.01..0.06) -- divide the reported quantity by 0.01 to recover the bin 1-6.
binQty = rewardDist < 500 ? 0.01 : rewardDist < 1000 ? 0.02 : rewardDist < 1500 ? 0.03 : rewardDist < 2000 ? 0.04 : rewardDist < 2500 ? 0.05 : 0.06

var int barsIn = 0

flat = strategy.position_size == 0

if flat and goLong
    strategy.entry("L", strategy.long, qty=binQty)
    barsIn := 0

if flat and goShort
    strategy.entry("S", strategy.short, qty=binQty)
    barsIn := 0

if strategy.position_size != 0
    barsIn := barsIn + 1

if barsIn >= 1 and strategy.position_size != 0
    strategy.close_all()
    barsIn := 0

plot(goLong  ? 1 : 0, title="LongSignal")
plot(goShort ? 1 : 0, title="ShortSignal")
plot(rewardDist, title="RewardDistance")
